# Loaded automatically by Expo CLI for any production build/export
# (NODE_ENV=production) — this is what a Release archive built directly
# through Xcode picks up when bundling JS, since that path never goes
# through `eas build`'s own env-var injection (see eas.json on other
# branches for the EAS-cloud-build equivalent of this same value).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the client bundle at build time and
# are not secret, so this is safe to commit.
#
# Without this file, a Release build silently falls back to apiClient.ts's
# DEFAULT_BASE_URL (http://localhost:3001) — unreachable on a real device,
# which is exactly the "no localhost/dev backend in Release" failure mode
# this file exists to prevent.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://shopsmart-backend-zl9l.onrender.com
